---
import Docs from "../layouts/Docs.astro";
import Code from "../components/Code.astro";
const generation = JSON.stringify(
  {
    schema_version: 3,
    request_id: "66f96fc9-969d-4c0e-ab92-e355fa0e7588",
    execution_mode: "native",
    project_dir: "/absolute/path/to/your-project",
    cli: "grok",
    model_selection: { kind: "native_default" },
    instructions:
      "Rewrite the supplied text for clarity. Return only the revision.",
    input: "Explain the tradeoffs of a cache for this application.",
    timeout_seconds: 120,
  },
  null,
  2,
);
const native = JSON.stringify(
  {
    action: "start",
    cli_name: "claude",
    project_dir: "/absolute/path/to/your-project",
    prompt: "Inspect the test suite and report which checks cover the parser.",
    request_key: "inspect-parser-tests-1",
    timeout_seconds: 180,
  },
  null,
  2,
);
---

<Docs
  title="Usage examples"
  description="Generate text from the shell, ask for advice through MCP, or delegate a native task that you can poll."
  toc={[
    ["generate", "Generate from a script"],
    ["consult", "Consult with Codex"],
    ["task", "Start a native task"],
  ]}
>
  <h2 id="generate">Generate from a script</h2>
  <p>
    This example uses a compatible, signed-in Grok Build installation and its
    native model default. From an existing project folder, approve that
    directory for Grok. The prompt defaults to No.
  </p>
  <Code
    label="Terminal · intended project"
    code={'clink allow "$(pwd -P)" --cli grok'}
  />
  <p>
    Save the following as <code>request.json</code>. Replace the example project
    path with the output of <code>pwd -P</code>. Give each new attempt a fresh
    UUID.
  </p>
  <Code label="request.json · schema 3" code={generation} />
  <Code
    label="Terminal"
    code="clink generate --request-json - < request.json"
  />
  <p>
    Clink reads one JSON object and writes a terminal result to stdout. Check
    for exit code 0 and <code>status: "completed"</code>. Validate the request
    ID and hashes before using the output. A failure is returned to the caller
    without an automatic retry or agent switch.
  </p>
  <h2 id="consult">Consult with Codex</h2>
  <p>
    In a connected MCP client, pass this object to the <code>clink</code> tool.
    Omitting the action selects an advisory consultation. This operation
    requires the verified Codex build.
  </p>
  <Code
    label="MCP · clink tool arguments"
    code={JSON.stringify(
      {
        cli_name: "codex",
        prompt:
          "Review this proposed change and suggest a clearer error message: a missing input currently returns “failed”.",
      },
      null,
      2,
    )}
  />
  <h2 id="task">Start a native task</h2>
  <p>
    To ask Claude Code to work in a project inside its configured roots, use the{" "}
    <code>start</code> action. Native agents use their own tools and permissions
    and can change files or call external services.
  </p>
  <Code label="MCP · clink tool arguments" code={native} />
  <p>
    Save the returned <code>task_handle</code>. Replace the placeholder below
    and pass the object to the same MCP tool to poll its state. See the{" "}
    <a href="/mcp/native-tasks/">native task guide</a> for follow-up,
    cancellation and restart behavior.
  </p>
  <Code
    label="MCP · poll the task"
    code={JSON.stringify(
      { action: "status", task_handle: "<returned task_handle>" },
      null,
      2,
    )}
  />
  <h2 id="repository">Ask a repository</h2>
  <p>
    Wrap one generation attempt in a function that checks the file references in
    the answer.{" "}
    <a href="/extensions/ask-repo/">Try the downloadable ask_repo example</a>.
  </p>
</Docs>
